TEXT 64 32 Left 2 ;Series RLC band-pass: step response
TEXT 64 656 Left 2 !.tran 0 1.2m 0 500n
TEXT 64 704 Left 2 ;VIN is a 0 to 1 V step. L and C set the natural frequency near 5.03 kHz.
TEXT 64 768 Left 2 ;1. Click Run: the running-person button at the top left.
TEXT 64 808 Left 2 ;2. On the schematic, click the wire labeled VOUT (not the component).
TEXT 64 848 Left 2 ;3. Click the VIN wire too, to compare input and output in the same plot.
TEXT 64 888 Left 2 ;If the plot is empty, select the schematic window and click the labeled wire again.
TEXT 64 968 Left 2 ;EXPERIMENTS AND COMMON QUESTIONS
TEXT 64 1008 Left 2 ;Right-click a component to edit its value. Predict first, change one value, then Run.
TEXT 64 1048 Left 2 ;VOUT is across R1. It starts near 0 V, rings, then returns to 0 V.
TEXT 64 1088 Left 2 ;TRY: Increase R1 to 680 ohms. Larger series R damps the ringing.
TEXT 64 1128 Left 2 ;WHY: Inductor current cannot jump, and the series capacitor blocks DC.
